This is a native BSD-make integration of the in-tree OpenSSL provider, not a
validated module. No host Configure/perl/gmake or target execution is required
by buildworld. The module is self-contained, exports only OSSL_provider_init,
and must not depend on libcrypto. Portable C implementations deliberately avoid
reusing libcrypto's non-FIPS objects or architecture-specific defines. Normal
libcrypto retains its existing assembly acceleration.

Makefile.sources is derived from the recursive sources of providers/libfips.a
and providers/fips in upstream configdata %unified_info, configured with:
  Configure BSD-x86_64 enable-fips no-asm no-tests no-acvp-tests
and base's disabled algorithms. Include ecp_nistp{224,256,384,521}.c and
ecp_nistputil.c: base's universal configuration enables these on 64-bit little
endian targets, and the source files guard unsupported targets themselves.
Keep the full source list, including upstream common implementation sources;
section garbage collection and the export map discard unreachable helpers.
Regenerate and rerun self-tests when importing OpenSSL. Do not mix source
versions or replace this module with a validated module without following that
module's Security Policy and rechecking application compatibility.

fips_build.h overrides only this provider's inherited disabled POST/security
checks and assembly selection. Base configuration disables ACVP test hooks.
All installed module transformations must precede fipsinstall provisioning.
The existing cache scans only top-level /lib and /usr/lib shared libraries, so
/usr/lib/ossl-modules/fips.so remains standalone.
